\title{novaRush: R Client for the Fluree v4 Graph Database}
\description{
Read from and write to a Fluree v4 ledger. Queries are composed with pipeable verbs and return tibbles; JSON-LD Query, SPARQL and history queries are all supported, as are signed messages, time travel and RDFS/OWL reasoning. Data goes in as a triple table, a 'tidygraph' graph or raw JSON-LD, and query results come back as a tibble or a graph. Ledger administration covers branches, named graphs, and storage and exact similarity search over native Fluree vectors. The lower-level R6 interface ('FlureeInstance' and friends) remains available for full control of the request cycle.
